  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 1.0,
      "text": "Right, 2048 in a terminal. Same game you already know, just printed out as text."
    },
    {
      "t": 9.0,
      "text": "First thing I always do is ask the thing what it even takes."
    },
    {
      "t": 14.0,
      "text": "Nothing clever. A handful of words, and it tells you off if a move wouldn't do anything."
    },
    {
      "t": 20.5,
      "text": "Let's have a look at what we've been dealt."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.0,
      "text": "Okay, so here's the whole trick, and it's a discipline rather than a clever move: you pick yourself a corner, you keep your biggest tile wedged into it, and you keep the row it sits in tidy so nothing can slip in behind it."
    },
    {
      "t": 42.5,
      "text": "Which in practice means you're pushing the same couple of ways over and over, and there's one direction you simply don't take."
    },
    {
      "t": 50.5,
      "text": "See how it all collects down into that corner."
    },
    {
      "t": 56.0,
      "text": "Keep going. Boring is the point."
    },
    {
      "t": 59.0,
      "text": "If that row stays tidy, things merge along it instead of scattering everywhere."
    },
    {
      "t": 64.22,
      "text": "I'll skip us ahead a bit here. It's the same few keys the whole way."
    },
    {
      "t": 69.07,
      "text": "And there's our big one, sat exactly where we left it."
    },
    {
      "t": 73.5,
      "text": "Now watch what happens if I get impatient and go the other way."
    },
    {
      "t": 78.0,
      "text": "Gone. Lifted clean off, bottom's empty, and you'll be unpicking that for the next fifty moves."
    },
    {
      "t": 85.0,
      "text": "If you genuinely are stuck, try the others first, costs you nothing, and then put it straight back."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Hermetic. Every terminal screen is verbatim stdout from the frozen interface (env/2048/v2s_game_2048.py) played on seed 716 -- a board the task does not provision, so the procedure has to be carried across boards rather than replayed. Narration is deliberately vague where the pixels are exact (docs/preregistration.md 7.2): it says there is a corner, a tidy row and a direction to avoid, and never which corner, which ordering or which direction. Those appear only on screen, so the transcript-only and raw-transcript arms are a fair representation of what narration alone carries."
}
